codex
The proof chain is sound—the invariant proof returned `#Top`—but the full theorem is currently spending time normalizing the recursive “all elements are positive” side condition on a symbolic tail. Since proving operational equivalence for all integer lists is stronger than restricting it to positive lists, I’m removing that redundant recursive precondition.
